Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:40:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 175/178] glm: TF_GLM_EXL3_BF16_SLOTS=1, a prompt chunk's fused
 EXL3 experts write bf16 slot rows (an NVFP4 chunk's form)

The prompt down kernel's fp32 slot rows were half its time at GLM-5.3's TP4 shape (4096 rows: 6.05 ms, 4.36 ms with bf16
stores) and the combine reads them again. Opt-in: different numerics.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
